    "presetPresentation": {
        "version": 1,
        "description": "Expressive saxophone: CC1 Attack and release; CC2 Brightness; CC3 Timbral onset; CC4 Air and rasp; CC5 Vibrato depth; CC11 Expression; CC76 Vibrato rate; CC77 Periodic roughness. Overlapping notes connect in Legato mode; separated notes articulate afresh. Play the embedded phrase for isolated controls and combinations.\n\nCC1 changes attack/release; note-off determines short-note duration.\nCC4 scales existing component noise; residual guide jitter remains at zero.\nCC77 is 25 Hz amplitude roughness, an unverified acoustic growl hypothesis.\nPitch is neutral at CC5 zero; full depth is approximately +/-30 cents.\nReference recordings do not establish observed source MIDI controls.",
        "tags": [ "Brass" ],
        "preview": {
